So here is my 3D model of the tablet

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.743
and one of the things that
I was working on is well,

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.660
the lighting we have right
now is really different

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.480
from the lighting back 3,000 years ago.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:29.690
So of course the tablet
is going to look different

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.660
if it's lit by modern
lights, versus if it's lit

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.150
by what they probably
had, like torch light.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:35.500
So I've been working on
some different models

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.543
of illumination using fire.

00:13:41.037 --> 00:13:42.510
So, like then you would be able to cycle

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.900
through these different kinds of lighting

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:48.130
and get a better idea of
what these tablets look like,

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.420
and one portion that I
am currently working on

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.780
where this affective
lighting is really going

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.920
to make a difference,
is that I'm working on

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:57.470
trying to reconstruct
what the original coloring

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:58.900
of these tablets would look like,

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.520
because these tablets were all

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:03.220
originally painted 3,000 years ago.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.850
If you go to the art
gallery, the other tablet,

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.660
at the art gallery you can
actually see like some red

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.660
still on the feet of the tablet.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:14.256
So we're working on
talking to art historians

00:14:14.256 --> 00:14:17.770
and conservators,

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:20.670
on what colors the tablet

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.250
would have looked like back then.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.860
And that's where the
lighting is really going

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.750
to make a big difference
because different colors

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.800
are gonna look really different
under kinds of lighting,

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:34.050
'cause it's most likely
that the kinds of colors

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:36.470
they are using would
look very garish today

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.640
under normal lighting
but under fire lighting

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.140
they'd being much more subdued

00:14:41.136 --> 00:14:45.093
and then more aesthetically
pleasing kind of image.

00:14:47.628 --> 00:14:50.961
(cheerful techno music)

